[177.62675, "o", "msam-node\u001b[38;5;189;49m is running locally, we can reach it without needing any tokens if we use its Unix socket. This is perfect for querying SAM's connected AI models.\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;189m\u001b[164X\u001b[m\n\u001b[38;5;189mFor instance, I just automatically queried \u001b[38;5;111;48;5;236m/v1/models\u001b[38;5;189;49m across the mesh and found two endpoints available:\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;189m\u001b[104X\u001b[m\n\u001b[38;5;189m• \u001b[38;5;111;48;5;236mgoogle/gemma-2-2b-it\u001b[m\n\u001b[20D\u001b[38;5;111;48;5;236mopenrouter/auto\u001b[38;5;189;49m     \u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;189m\u001b[17X\u001b[m\n\u001b[38;5;189mWe can send a chat completion request directly to a mesh model. Here's an example you can run straight in your terminal to see it in action:\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;189m\u001b[140X\u001b[m\n\u001b[2C\u001b[38;5;251mcurl --unix-socket ~/.config/sam-mesh/sam.sock \u001b[38;5;158m\\\u001b[m\n\u001b[48D\u001b[38;5;251m  \u001b]8;id=jke32253df;http://localhost/v1/chat/completions\u0007http://localhost/v1/chat/completions\u001b]8;;\u0007 \u001b[38;5;158m\\\u001b[38;5;189m        \u001b[m\n\u001b[46D\u001b[38;5;251m-H \u001b[38;5;173m'Content-Type: application/json'\u001b[38;5;251m \u001b[38;5;158m\\\u001b[38;5;189m"]
[177.626759, "o", " \u001b[m\n\u001b[37D\u001b[38;5;251md \u001b[38;5;173m'{\"model\": \"google/gemma-2-2b-it\", \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Hello from the SAM mesh demo!\"}]}'\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[4C\u001b[38;5;189m\u001b[116X\u001b[m\n\b\b\u001b[38;5;39;1m### 2. Discovering remote APIs and Tools\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;189m\u001b[40X\u001b[m\n\u001b[38;5;189mYou can give agents (like me!) access to networked tools. The mesh nodes discover these using the MCP (Model Context Protocol). Here's how to configure me to have first-class\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;189maccess to any tools running on the mesh endpoints so I don't have to \u001b[38;5;111;48;5;236mcurl\u001b[38;5;189;49m:\u001b[100X\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;189m\u001b[74X\u001b[m\n\u001b[38;5;189m1. Open your Antigravity MCP settings: \u001b[38;5;111;48;5;236m~/.gemini/config/mcp_config.json\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;189m2. Add the SAM MCP server using the node API token we just generated (which is safely tucked away in \u001b[38;5;111;48;5;236m~/.config/sam-mesh/api-token\u001b[38;5;189;49m):\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;189m\u001b[131X\u001b[m\n\u001b[2C\u001b[38;5;187m{\u001b[38;5;189m \u001b[m\n\b\b\u001b[38;5;251m  \u001b[38;5;140m\"mcpServers\"\u001b[38;5;187m:\u001b[38;5;251m \u001b[38;5;187m{\u001b[m\n\u001b"]
[177.626768, "o", "[15D\u001b[38;5;251m  \u001b[38;5;140m\"sam-mesh\u001b[m\r\n\t\u001b[38;5;251m  \u001b[38;5;140m\"serverUrl\"\u001b[38;5;187m:\u001b[38;5;251m \u001b[38;5;173m\"\u001b]8;id=jk72e0e2d5;http://127.0.0.1:8080/mcp\u0007http://127.0.0.1:8080/mcp\u001b]8;;\u0007\"\u001b[38;5;187m,\u001b[m\n\u001b[40D\u001b[38;5;140mheaders\"\u001b[38;5;187m:\u001b[38;5;251m \u001b[38;5;187m{\u001b[38;5;189m\u001b[29X\u001b[m\n\u001b[12D\u001b[38;5;251m \u001b[38;5;189m       \u001b[m\n\n\n\u001b[16D\u001b[?25h"]
